From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] interdrv: cvi_vc_drv: fail SendFrame without encoder buffers

The first H.264/H.265 frame registers the reconstruction buffers
(CVI_H26X_OP_REG_VB_BUFFER) but its result was ignored: when the video
heap could not hold them, encoding went on and cviEncode265Header faulted
in __memcpy on the missing bitstream buffer (kernel Oops in the capture
thread; the heap stays allocated until a reboot). Return
CVI_ERR_VENC_NOBUF instead, so the caller can destroy the channel.

---
diff --git a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/module/src/cvi_venc.c b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/module/src/cvi_venc.c
index ee54c4c..5945b08 100644
--- a/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/module/src/cvi_venc.c
+++ b/interdrv/cvi_vc_drv/module/src/cvi_venc.c
@@ -2414,7 +2414,17 @@ CVI_S32 CVI_VENC_SendFrame(VENC_CHN VeChn, const VIDEO_FRAME_INFO_S *pstFrame,
 
 		if (pChnHandle->pChnAttr->stVencAttr.enType == PT_H264 ||
 		    pChnHandle->pChnAttr->stVencAttr.enType == PT_H265) {
-			_cviVencRegVbBuf(VeChn);
+			/* Without its reconstruction buffers (or the bitstream
+			 * buffer allocated before them) the encoder must not
+			 * run: encoding the headers reads the missing
+			 * bitstream buffer and faults in __memcpy. Report the
+			 * shortage; the caller destroys the channel. */
+			s32Ret = _cviVencRegVbBuf(VeChn);
+			if (s32Ret != CVI_SUCCESS) {
+				CVI_VENC_ERR("_cviVencRegVbBuf, %d
+", s32Ret);
+				return CVI_ERR_VENC_NOBUF;
+			}
 		}
 
 		pChnVars->u32FirstPixelFormat =
